summary: proc/stat stops updating when nohz_full set
description: |
    Check /proc/stat to see if it still keep updating when nohz_full
    is setup.

    the time cost on checking the cpu stat is scaled by  processor
    number, extend the max_runtime when running large-cpu machine.
    it's rather slow on kernel-rt-debug, a 64 processor will cost 15s
    each loop.
contact: Chunyu Hu <chuhu@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - gcc
  - libgcc
  - glibc-devel
  - rpm-build
  - psmisc
  - wget
recommend:
  - rt-setup
  - realtime-setup
  - trace-cmd
duration: 4h
extra-summary: kernel/general/scheduler/1423560-nohz-proc-stat-stop-update
extra-task: kernel/general/scheduler/1423560-nohz-proc-stat-stop-update
